+    """rho0 = 1, g = 1, L = 2 pi, mu = g rho0: the Hessian of E - mu N has eigenvalues
+    k^2/2 + 2 g rho0 for k = 0, +-1, ...; on the sphere the k = 0 mode (psi0 itself)
+    is removed."""
+    grid = dipgpe.Grid(64, 2 * math.pi, dtype=C128, device=DEVICE)
